{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>judge me</b> — take up my case against those who taunt me, and they are many; therefore he said: \"from a nation.\"" "And the meaning of <b>not a devout man</b> — because I am better than he." "And the meaning of <b>from a man</b> — from general and particular, or an allusion to the one who rules over the nation."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:36.981745111Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}